# English audience and product naming

Chinaready Landscape targets **English-speaking readers**. Write page copy, meta, FAQ, guide text, and editorial overrides in English.

## Chinese product / brand names

Lead with the English (or Latin) name. Put the Chinese name in parentheses when it helps recognition.

```text
✅ Jingbei Guanjia (经贝管家)
✅ Pangle (穿山甲)
✅ Umeng+ (友盟+)

❌ 经贝管家 (Jingbei Guanjia)
❌ Leading with Chinese characters in running English copy
```

## Practical rules

- First mention: `English Name (中文名)` when a Chinese label is useful.
- Later mentions: prefer the English name alone unless the Chinese form is needed for clarity.
- Do not use bare Chinese product names as the primary label in English pages, titles, tables, or FAQs.
- Keep Chinese inside parentheses, quotes for official notices, or proper nouns that have no stable English form — still introduce them with an English lead-in when possible.
